WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Music has the power to change our mood instantly.
音乐有力量瞬间改变我们的情绪。

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Think about the last time you heard your favorite song.
想想上次你听到最喜欢的歌曲时的情景。

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Did you notice how your spirits lifted?
你注意到你的情绪是如何提升的吗？

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:19.000
This is not just in your head; it is actually happening in your brain.
这不仅仅是你的感觉；它实际上正在你的大脑中发生。

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:25.000
When we listen to music, our brain releases dopamine, a neurotransmitter that makes us feel pleasure and reward.
当我们听音乐时，我们的大脑释放多巴胺，这是一种让我们感到愉悦和奖励的神经递质。

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:32.000
This is the same chemical that is released when we eat delicious food, exercise, or experience something enjoyable.
这与我们在吃美食、锻炼或体验愉快事物时释放的化学物质相同。

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:37.000
The release of dopamine explains why music can make us feel so good.
多巴胺的释放解释了为什么音乐能让我们感觉如此良好。

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:43.000
Studies suggest that music can improve memory and learning abilities.
研究表明，音乐可以提高记忆力和学习能力。

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:49.000
Researchers have found that students who study music tend to perform better academically than those who do not.
研究人员发现，学习音乐的学生在学业上的表现往往优于不学习音乐的学生。

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:55.000
This is because learning to play an instrument requires focus, discipline, and the coordination of multiple brain regions.
这是因为学习演奏乐器需要专注、自律和多个大脑区域的协调。

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:01.000
Not only does music entertain us, but it also stimulates brain activity across multiple areas.
音乐不仅娱乐我们，而且还刺激多个大脑区域的活动。

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:07.000
When you listen to music, your auditory cortex processes the sound.
当你听音乐时，你的听觉皮层处理声音。

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Your motor cortex wants to move to the rhythm, and your limbic system processes the emotions.
你的运动皮层想要跟随节奏移动，你的边缘系统处理情绪。

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:17.000
All of this happens simultaneously, making music a truly full-brain experience.
所有这些都同时发生，使音乐成为真正的全脑体验。

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:22.000
This is because music is uniquely complex.
这是因为音乐具有独特的复杂性。

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:28.000
It combines melody, harmony, rhythm, and lyrics, each processed by different parts of the brain.
它结合了旋律、和声、节奏和歌词，每一个都由大脑的不同部分处理。

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:34.000
This comprehensive activation may explain why music is so effective at enhancing cognitive function.
这种全面的激活可能解释了为什么音乐在增强认知功能方面如此有效。

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:40.000
Different types of music have different effects on our emotions.
不同类型的音乐对我们的情绪有不同的影响。

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:46.000
Fast-paced music with a strong beat can increase energy and motivation, which is why many people listen to upbeat music during exercise.
节奏强劲的快速音乐可以增加能量和动力，这就是为什么许多人在锻炼时听欢快的音乐。

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:53.000
Slow, calm music with a gentle melody promotes relaxation and reduces stress, making it ideal for unwinding after a long day.
旋律柔和的缓慢、平静的音乐促进放松和减轻压力，使其成为长时间工作后放松的理想选择。

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:59.000
Music therapy is increasingly used in hospitals, schools, and rehabilitation centers.
音乐治疗越来越多地用于医院、学校和康复中心。

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:06.000
Therapists use music to help patients recover from brain injuries, manage pain, reduce anxiety, and improve communication skills.
治疗师使用音乐帮助患者从脑损伤中恢复、管理疼痛、减少焦虑和改善沟通技巧。

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:12.000
In some cases, patients who cannot speak due to brain damage can still sing, demonstrating the powerful connection between music and the brain.
在某些情况下，由于脑损伤无法说话的患者仍然可以唱歌，这展示了音乐与大脑之间的强大联系。

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:18.000
As a result, incorporating music into daily life can enhance our well-being in numerous ways.
因此，将音乐融入日常生活可以在许多方面提升我们的幸福感。

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:24.000
Whether you are studying, working, exercising, or simply relaxing, music can improve your performance and mood.
无论你是在学习、工作、锻炼还是只是放松，音乐都可以改善你的表现和情绪。

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:30.000
In other words, music is not just entertainment.
换句话说，音乐不仅仅是娱乐。

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:37.000
It is a powerful tool that can enhance our cognitive abilities, improve our emotional health, and enrich our lives.
它是一个强大的工具，可以增强我们的认知能力，改善我们的情绪健康，丰富我们的生活。

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:43.000
So go ahead, turn on your favorite playlist, and let your brain enjoy the many benefits of music.
所以，打开你最喜欢的播放列表，让你的大脑享受音乐的诸多好处吧。
